  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside and the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype, mediated through the enzyme Cytochrome c4. This relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, all of which indicate that kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside acts as a target for Cytochrome c4, which in turn targets the EP4 receptor. The consistent scores across the three paths (final_score=0.6061) suggest a strong, reliable connection, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence highlights a network of targets that converge on the EP4 receptor, implying that kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside may influence the receptor through multiple pathways, possibly by modulating the activity of Cytochrome c4. The findings underscore the importance of Cytochrome c4 as a central node in this biological pathway, reinforcing the potential role of kaempferol 3-O-rhamnoside in regulating EP4 receptor function."
